1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,333
Hour sixty. You wake up to silence.
The window is blue.

2
00:00:04,033 --> 00:00:06,867
It's over. Look at that sky. Home is
three hours away.

3
00:00:07,567 --> 00:00:12,433
The stove is out of wood. The road
home runs straight across one giant,
shining slope.

4
00:00:13,133 --> 00:00:16,133
No food. No fire. A perfect blue sky.
Would you walk?

5
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:22,233
Rule nine. The first blue sky is the
deadliest hour. New snow needs time to
settle.

6
00:00:22,933 --> 00:00:29,567
Avalanches love the clear day after a
big storm. And in most deadly slides,
the victims set them off themselves.

7
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:32,500
Three hours from home, and you want to
sit?

8
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:36,200
I just found you. I'm not losing you
to good weather.
